<!--
    Swift's calling convention on methods and witnesses (`option swiftcall
    on|off`, the calling-convention arm of `swiftmetadata`).

    Issue: Swift passes a method's `self` in the swiftself register (r13 on
    x86-64, x20 on arm64) and a throwing function's error in the swifterror
    register (r12 / x21), which the C model neither reads as a parameter nor
    hands back from a call. A method's `self` is an unnamed register read
    (`int8 *v3; // r13`), a call drops the `self` it passes, and a caller's
    test of the error register after a throwing call reads the zero it
    stored before it, so `try?`'s error path folds away. Only a getter,
    whose arity is known, had its `self` typed (8,560 on the Toyota iOS app).

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, the Swift metadata pass
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/swift/kuna_swiftcall.rs`), with the model
    binding read in P4 (`ActionDefaultParams`, the decompile drive) and the
    `self` hint in P5 type inference.

    P0 assertion: `option swiftcall on|off` (default on; inert unless
    `swiftmetadata` is on).

    The fixtures are one swiftc 6.3 build of `swift_call_elf.swift`:
    `swift_call_elf` stripped, `swift_call_syms_elf` with its symbols. Pass 1
    (`option swiftcall off`, stripped) reproduces the BUG: the class method
    `vtable#7.method` (`deposit(_:fee:)`) takes two parameters and reads its
    `self` from an unnamed `r13`, the struct witness reads `v1 + 8`, and
    `run` returns the throwing call's result unchecked. Pass 2 (the
    default, stripped) is the FIX: the method takes `callfix.Account *self`
    first, the struct witness writes `self->step`, the class witness takes
    `callfix.Account **self` (a witness gets the address of the value), and
    `run` keeps the error path (`if (v5) { swift_release(v5); v3 = -1; }`)
    and passes `self` to the throwing virtual call. Pass 3 (the default,
    with symbols) types the mutating struct method by its name
    (`callfix.Counter.advance(by:times:)(callfix.Counter *self,...)`) and
    `run`'s call passes it `self`, while the non-mutating `peek`, whose
    `self` is exploded into its trailing arguments, gains none.
-->
